  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this proposal is to establish local capacity within governmental and non-governmental sectors to effectively monitor and conserve tiger and prey populations. This will be done by: 1) training and empowering local forest department personnel in rigorous monitoring of tigers through camera trap based capture-recapture sampling and monitoring of prey through line transect based Distance sampling in Wayanad Wildlife Sanctuary; 2) collaborating with other organizations with similar conservation agendas active in Kerala to build local capacity through intensive training in field survey activities, workshops and awareness programs; and 3) proactively involving members of the civil society in tiger prey estimation and monitoring activities.</narrative>
  </description>
